The downloaded files are organized in the following way:
- Summary_table.csv: the table with the results of the muon resting sites search, after the clustering. Format is CSV;
- Supercell_#.cif: supercells hosting the muon site (each label # corresponding to the "label" in the tables). Format is cif.
- Allsites_unitcell.cif: the unit cell of the system with all the muon sites of Summary_table.csv together.
- Distortion_supercell_#.csv: summary of the muon-induced distortion of the atoms with respect to their initial and final distance from the muon. Format is CSV.
- Summary_table_before_clustering.csv: the table with the results of the muon resting sites search before clustering. Format is CSV;
- Allsites_before_clustering_unitcell.cif: the undistorted unit cell of the system with all the muon sites together before clustering.
- Allsites_before_clustering_supercell.cif: the undistorted supercell of the system with all the muon sites together before clustering.


## About the summary tables:

The table collects the results of the muon resting sites search. Each row is a muon site. The different columns show:
- "supercell_index" (first column): the id of the relaxation, i.e. of the supercell, of the muon site. It starts from 0. It is NOT the position of the site in the table, and it is unrelated to the "label" and to the energy order.
- "structure_id_pk": the AiiDA id (or pk) of the relaxed supercell structure in the database.
- "label": a label for the given site, and for its supercell file (Supercell_#.cif): a letter, in order of increasing energy (A is the lowest energy site).
- "delta_E": the total energy difference with respect to the lowest energy (meV).
- "tot_energy": the total energy of the calculation (meV).
- "muon_position_cc": the position of the muon in the supercell (crystal coordinates).
{% if B_fields %}
- "B_T": the total magnetic field at the muon site (dipolar and hyperfine contributions).
- "Bdip": the dipolar magnetic field at the muon site.
- "B_T_norm": the norm of the total magnetic field.
- "Bdip_norm": the norm of the dipolar magnetic field.
- "B_hf_norm": the norm of the hyperfine magnetic field.
{% endif %}
- "atom_index_in_unit_cell": the number of the muon atom in the unit cell with all the muon sites, i.e. in the file Allsites_unitcell.cif for Summary_table.csv and in the file Allsites_before_clustering_unitcell.cif for Summary_table_before_clustering.csv. It is 1-based: the first atom of the cif file is atom 1. Please check that your visualizer is 1-based. ASE and Python are 0-based, so there use "atom_index_in_unit_cell" minus 1. Note that "supercell_index", instead, starts from 0.

In the "Summary_table_before_clustering.csv" table there will be also the information about the clustering: the last column, called "cluster group", is a number (starting from 1) that identifies the group to which the muon site belongs: the sites with the same number belong to the same group. The sites of the table "Summary_table.csv" are the representative sites of the groups.


## About the clustering:

The clustering algorithm used has two steps:
1. muon sites that are closer than 0.5 Angstrom, and whose energies differ by less than 0.05 eV, are considered the same site. The "cluster group" column of "Summary_table_before_clustering.csv" reports this grouping;
2. the sites that are equivalent by the symmetry of the host (within 0.05 Angstrom) and whose energies differ by less than 0.05 eV are merged too.
The sites that remain are those of "Summary_table.csv".

## About the distortion_supercell_#.csv files:

The position of the muon considered is only the final relaxed one. We consider no physical meaning for the initial muon position: it just belongs to a grid of point used as initial guess. 
The columns of the file are:
- "atm_distance_init": the distance of the muon from the atoms of the unrelaxed supercell.
- "atm_distance_final": the distance of the muon from the atoms of the relaxed supercell.
- "distortion": i.e. the magnitude of the vector computed as the difference between the final and initial distance vectors.
- "delta_distances": radial displacement change, i.e. the difference between the magnitudes of the final and initial distances from the muon site.
- "element": the element of the atom.
